# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere for project-owned files.
# Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf=true by default; this
# file makes checkout deterministic regardless of client config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Corpus fixtures and oracle snapshots are byte-exact data: git must
# never apply line-ending conversion to them. With core.autocrlf=true
# (the windows-2022 runner image default), text-shaped snapshots under
# corpus/extract were checked out as CRLF, which broke the
# secondary_archives extract-parity tests on Windows CI.
corpus/** -text

# Vendored upstream trees must remain byte-identical to the pinned
# upstream commits (AGENTS.md: rules are stored as-is, no formatting
# or manual modification). Never convert their line endings; files
# upstream stores as CRLF stay CRLF.
upstream/** -text
